{"id":"QB-261020-EAZX","title":"Phiếu bài tập 03/10/2026","student":"Thomas","questions":[{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2025MAY-INT-A-M1-Q19","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2025MAY-INT-A-M1-Q19","label":"1","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"What is the $y$-intercept of the graph of $y=14^x$ in the $xy$-plane?","options":{"A":"$(0,15)$","B":"$(0,14)$","C":"$(0,1)$","D":"$(0,-1)$"}},{"id":"SAT-CB-PT8-M1-Q06","ref":"SAT-CB-PT8-M1-Q06","label":"2","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"$2.6 + x = 2.8$<br>What value of $x$ is the solution to the given equation?"},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-N-M1-Q15","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-N-M1-Q15","label":"3","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"Sonja purchased a laptop in September when the laptop had a value of \\$1,000. Each month for the next 50 months, the value of the laptop decreased by 2% of the previous month's value. Which equation represents this situation, where $v$ is the value of the laptop, in dollars, $m$ is the number of months since Sonja purchased the laptop, and $m\\le50$?","options":{"A":"$v=2{,}019(0.98)^m$","B":"$v=2{,}019(2)^m$","C":"$v=1{,}000(0.98)^m$","D":"$v=1{,}000(2)^m$"}},{"id":"PSAT-EQB-20261018-PSDA-Q45","ref":"PSAT-EQB-20261018-PSDA-Q45","label":"4","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"The table summarizes the distribution of age and assigned group for $90$ participants in a study.<br>$$\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline & \\text{0-9 years} & \\text{10-19 years} & \\text{20+ years} & \\text{Total}\\\\\\hline \\text{Group A} & 5 & 17 & 8 & 30\\\\\\hline \\text{Group B} & 6 & 8 & 16 & 30\\\\\\hline \\text{Group C} & 19 & 5 & 6 & 30\\\\\\hline \\text{Total} & 30 & 30 & 30 & 90\\\\\\hline\\end{array}$$<br>One of these participants will be selected at random. What is the probability of selecting a participant from group A, given that the participant is at least $10$ years of age?","options":{"A":"$\\dfrac{5}{18}$","B":"$\\dfrac{5}{12}$","C":"$\\dfrac{17}{30}$","D":"$\\dfrac{5}{6}$"}},{"id":"SAT-CB-PT7-M2-Q22","ref":"SAT-CB-PT7-M2-Q22","label":"5","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"$\\begin{array}{cc} x & f(x) \\\\ -4 & 0 \\\\ -\\dfrac{19}{5} & 1 \\\\ -\\dfrac{18}{5} & 2 \\end{array}$<br><br>For the linear function $f$, the table shows three values of $x$ and their corresponding values of $f(x)$. If $h(x) = f(x) - 13$, which equation defines $h$ ?","options":{"A":"$h(x) = 5x - 4$","B":"$h(x) = 5x + 7$","C":"$h(x) = 5x + 9$","D":"$h(x) = 5x + 20$"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-M-M2-Q16","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-M-M2-Q16","label":"6","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"The function $T(x)=66-8x$ estimates the temperature, in degrees Fahrenheit ($^\\circ$F), in a certain city one day in January, where $x$ is the number of hours after 10 a.m. and $1\\le x\\le7$. Which statement is the best interpretation of $T(6)=18$ in this context?","options":{"A":"6 hours after 10 a.m., the function estimates that the temperature is $18^\\circ$F.","B":"6 hours before 10 a.m., the function estimates that the temperature decreased $18^\\circ$F.","C":"6 hours after 10 a.m., the function estimates that the temperature decreased $18^\\circ$F.","D":"6 hours before 10 a.m., the function estimates that the temperature is $18^\\circ$F."}},{"id":"PSAT-2026-P89-PT3-M1-Q13","ref":"PSAT-2026-P89-PT3-M1-Q13","label":"7","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"$3x + 8y = 68$<br>$y = 7$<br><br>The solution to the given system of equations is $(x, y)$. What is the value of $x$?"},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-N-M1-Q09","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-N-M1-Q09","label":"8","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"The function $v(t)=9t+70$ gives the volume of water, in liters, in a tank being filled by a hose $t$ minutes after the hose was turned on. Which of the following is the best interpretation of 70 in this context?","options":{"A":"The volume of water in the tank increases at a rate of 70 liters per minute.","B":"The tank holds a maximum of 70 liters.","C":"It takes 70 hours to fill the tank completely.","D":"There were 70 liters of water in the tank when the hose was turned on."}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-A-M1-Q19","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-A-M1-Q19","label":"9","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"The value, in dollars, of a certain bicycle $t$ years after it was purchased can be modeled by the function $f(t)=160(0.93)^{t}$. According to the model, what was the estimated value, in dollars, of the bicycle when it was purchased?"},{"id":"PSAT-2024-P89-PT2-M2-Q13","ref":"PSAT-2024-P89-PT2-M2-Q13","label":"10","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"$x^{2} = (22)(22)$<br><br>What is the positive solution to the given equation?"},{"id":"SAT-CB-PT7-M1-Q01","ref":"SAT-CB-PT7-M1-Q01","label":"11","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"The scatterplot shows the temperature, in degrees Fahrenheit (°F), and the distance above sea level, in feet, measured at 6 locations on Mount Jefferson. A line of best fit is also shown. At a distance of 4,000 feet above sea level, what is the temperature, in °F, predicted by the line of best fit?","options":{"A":"47","B":"35","C":"25","D":"0"},"figures":[{"src":"data:image/png;base64,","alt":"Scatterplot with a line of best fit. Horizontal axis 'Distance above sea level (feet)', labelled 2,000, 4,000, 6,000, 8,000. Vertical axis 'Temperature (°F)', labelled 10 to 80 in steps of 10. Six data points about: (1,000, 48), (2,000, 38), (3,000, 38), (5,000, 35), (6,000, 25), (7,000, 26). The straight line of best fit starts at about 47 on the vertical axis at 0 feet and falls to about 20 near 8,900 feet; at 4,000 feet it is at about 35."}]},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026MAR-US-B-M1-Q12","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026MAR-US-B-M1-Q12","label":"12","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"For the exponential function $g$, the value of $g(x)$ doubles for every increase of $2$ in the value of $x$. If $g(4)=9$, what is the value of $g(6)$?"},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-A-M1-Q21","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-A-M1-Q21","label":"13","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"Triangle $ABC$ is a right triangle with right angle at $B$. If the length of side $AC$ is 13 and the length of side $AB$ is 5, what is the value of $\\sin C$?","options":{"A":"$\\frac{5}{13}$","B":"$\\frac{12}{13}$","C":"$\\frac{5}{12}$","D":"$\\frac{13}{5}$"}},{"id":"PSAT-EQB-20261018-SALG-Q29","ref":"PSAT-EQB-20261018-SALG-Q29","label":"14","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"A local transit company sells a monthly pass for \\$95 that allows an unlimited number of trips of any length. Tickets for individual trips cost \\$1.50, \\$2.50, or \\$3.50, depending on the length of the trip. What is the minimum number of trips per month for which a monthly pass could cost less than purchasing individual tickets for trips?"},{"id":"SAT-CB-PT7-M2-Q27","ref":"SAT-CB-PT7-M2-Q27","label":"15","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"$y = -2.5$<br>$y = x^2 + 8x + k$<br><br>In the given system of equations, $k$ is a positive integer constant. The system has no real solutions. What is the least possible value of $k$ ?"},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-N-M1-Q20","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-N-M1-Q20","label":"16","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"The minimum value of $x$ is $4$ less than $7$ times another number $n$. Which inequality shows the possible values of $x$?","options":{"A":"$x\\le7n-4$","B":"$x\\ge7n-4$","C":"$x\\le4-7n$","D":"$x\\ge4-7n$"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2025MAY-INT-A-M1-Q04","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2025MAY-INT-A-M1-Q04","label":"17","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"A company opens an account with an initial balance of \\$35,600.00. The account earns interest, and no additional deposits or withdrawals are made. The account balance is given by an exponential function $A$, where $A(t)$ is the account balance, in dollars, $t$ years after the account is opened. The account balance after $15$ years is \\$129,672.38. Which equation could define $A$?","options":{"A":"$A(t)=35,600.00(1.09)^t$","B":"$A(t)=35,600.00(0.09)^t$","C":"$A(t)=94,072.38(1.09)^t$","D":"$A(t)=94,072.38(0.09)^t$"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2025OCT-INT-A-M2-Q13","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2025OCT-INT-A-M2-Q13","label":"18","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"For the linear function $f$, $f(1)=654$ and $f(2)=648$. Which of the following defines $f$?","options":{"A":"$f(x)=\\frac{1}{6}x+\\frac{3{,}923}{6}$","B":"$f(x)=-\\frac{1}{6}x+\\frac{3{,}925}{6}$","C":"$f(x)=6x+648$","D":"$f(x)=-6x+660$"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-D-M1-Q17","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-D-M1-Q17","label":"19","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"The expression $\\frac{kx-42}{2x^2-11x+15}$ is equivalent to $\\frac{p}{x-3}-\\frac{1}{2x-5}$, where $k$ and $p$ are constants. What is the value of $k$?","options":{"A":"$-41$","B":"$\\frac{39}{5}$","C":"$9$","D":"$17$"}},{"id":"SAT-CB-PT9-M1-Q06","ref":"SAT-CB-PT9-M1-Q06","label":"20","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"Each value in the data set shown represents the height, in centimeters, of a plant.<br>$6, 10, 13, 2, 15, 22, 10, 4, 4, 4$<br>What is the mean height, in centimeters, of these plants?"},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-B-M2-Q15","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-B-M2-Q15","label":"21","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"The function $f$ is defined by $f(x) = 6x - 3$. If $f(a) + 1 = 5a$, what is the value of $a$?","options":{"A":"$-1$","B":"$1$","C":"$2$","D":"$11$"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026MAR-INT-A-M1-Q06","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026MAR-INT-A-M1-Q06","label":"22","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"An object traveled $0.20$ meters for every $4.0$ seconds it was in motion. If the object was in motion for $24$ seconds, what is the total distance, in meters, the object traveled?"},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026MAR-INT-C-M2-Q21","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026MAR-INT-C-M2-Q21","label":"23","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"Trapezoid $ABCD$ is similar to trapezoid $EFGH$, where $A$, $B$, $C$, and $D$ correspond to $E$, $F$, $G$, and $H$, respectively. The area of trapezoid $ABCD$ is $440$ square inches, and the area of trapezoid $EFGH$ is $11,000$ square inches. The length of side $AB$ is $55$ inches. What is the length, in inches, of side $EF$?<br><br>Trapezoid $ABCD$ is similar to trapezoid $EFGH$, where $A$, $B$, $C$, and $D$ correspond to $E$, $F$, $G$, and $H$, respectively. The length of side $AB$ is $55$ inches. What is the length, in inches, of side $EF$?"},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-K-M1-Q08","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2026JUN-INT-K-M1-Q08","label":"24","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"$x+y=300$<br>The given equation relates the total number of bur oak trees, $x$, and the total number of other oak trees, $y$, planted in a 12-acre forest preserve. If 270 bur oak trees were planted in the forest preserve, how many other oak trees were planted in the forest preserve?","options":{"A":"270","B":"30","C":"25","D":"12"}},{"id":"SAT-RONAN-2025OCT-INT-A-M1-Q20","ref":"SAT-RONAN-2025OCT-INT-A-M1-Q20","label":"25","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"A linear model estimates the population of a city from $1992$ to $2016$. The model estimates the population was $61$ thousand in $1992$, $217$ thousand in $2012$, and $x$ thousand in $2016$. To the nearest whole number, what is the value of $x$?"}]}